    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0485" n="1445" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1445"/>

                <head>No. 981.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Curry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 28,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 272.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Supplementing my instruction No. 271, of
                    even date herewith, I inclose copies of correspondence between this Department
                    and the United States consul-general at Havana, concerning discriminating
                    tonnage dues collected by the customs authorities at Havana from the American
                    steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Jeanie</hi> in October last.</p>
                <p>From these papers, it will be seen that in identical cases of a Spanish and an
                    American vessel proceeding from one insular port to another in ballast before
                    departing on the final voyage to the United States, the difference of treatment
                    is conspicuous.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>









